            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Division by $x^2$ means that the required coefficient is the coefficient of $x^{m+2}$ in the numerator. In $(1+x)^j$, the general term is\n$$\\begin{align*}T_k&=\\binom{j}{k}x^k.\\end{align*}$$\nThe $x^{m+2}$ term has $k=m+2$ and occurs only when $j\\ge m+2$. Thus, for $1\\le m\\le n-2$, the coefficient is\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\sum_{j=m+2}^{n}\\binom{j}{m+2}\\\\C&=\\binom{m+2}{m+2}+\\binom{m+3}{m+2}+\\cdots+\\binom{n}{m+2}.\\end{align*}$$\nIf $m=n-1$ or $m=n$, then $m+2>n$, so no expansion contributes and the coefficient is $0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
